(EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK - 2023 EDITION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Meridian Logistics Group - Human Resources, Document HR-HB-2023) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Introduction) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This handbook summarizes the employment terms, benefits and workplace rules for all) Tj T*
(employees of Meridian Logistics Group. It is reviewed by Human Resources and replaces all) Tj T*
(earlier editions. Where an employment contract differs from this handbook, the contract) Tj T*
(prevails.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Working Hours and Remote Work) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Standard working time is 40 hours per week, Monday to Friday. Employees may work remotely up) Tj T*
(to 2 days per week with their manager's approval. Core collaboration hours are 10:00 to) Tj T*
(15:00, during which employees are expected to be reachable.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Leave and Vacation) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Full-time employees receive 24 paid vacation days per calendar year, in addition to public) Tj T*
(holidays. Unused vacation days may be carried into the first quarter of the following year.) Tj T*
(Sick leave requires a medical certificate from the third consecutive day of absence.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Probation and Notice Periods) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The probation period for new employees is 6 months. During probation, either party may) Tj T*
(terminate employment with two weeks' notice. After probation, statutory notice periods) Tj T*
(apply.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Offices) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The company maintains offices in Berlin. Desk booking is required for all locations and) Tj T*
(available through the facilities portal.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Conduct) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Employees are expected to act with integrity, protect confidential information, and follow) Tj T*
(the IT acceptable-use policy. Violations are handled by Human Resources and may lead to) Tj T*
(disciplinary measures.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
